# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The cell below imports the required tools and defines the helper functions used to analyze the results. The functions that build the circuit are defined step by step in the small-scale example below.\n"
msgstr "Ini-import ng cell sa ibaba ang mga kinakailangang tool at dine-define ang mga helper function na ginagamit sa pag-analyze ng mga resulta. Ang mga function na bumubuo ng circuit ay dine-define nang hakbang-hakbang sa small-scale na halimbawa sa ibaba.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each circuit stores its measurement outcomes in up to four classical registers:\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat circuit ay nag-iimbak ng mga resulta ng pagsukat nito sa hanggang apat na classical register:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`fusion`: the parity measurements used to fuse the GHZ patches\n"
msgstr "`fusion`: ang mga pagsukat ng parity na ginagamit para pagsamahin ang mga GHZ patch\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`ghz`: the GHZ readout bits that herald the W state (the root of each pair, or every GHZ qubit with no error detection)\n"
msgstr "`ghz`: ang mga GHZ readout bit na nagpapahiwatig ng W state (ang root ng bawat pares, o bawat GHZ qubit kapag walang error detection)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`flag`: the DisCo ED check bits (one per pair; not present without error detection)\n"
msgstr "`flag`: ang mga DisCo ED check bit (isa kada pares; wala kapag walang error detection)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`w`: the final measurement of the W qubits\n"
msgstr "`w`: ang huling pagsukat ng mga W qubit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The analysis has three steps. `postselect` keeps only the shots that pass the DisCo ED check (`flag` is cross-checked with `ghz`) and that herald the odd-parity sector (an odd number of 1s in `ghz`). The kept `w` bits then give the Hamming-weight distribution, the coherence $C$, and bounds on the fidelity $F$ with $|W_n\\rangle$. Finally, `exact_reference` gives the ideal values derived in the Background section. (If the circuits were built with `feedforward=False`, `postselect` first applies the GHZ corrections that were left for postprocessing. See Step 1 below.)\n"
msgstr "May tatlong hakbang ang analysis. Ang `postselect` ay nagtatago lang ng mga shot na pumasa sa DisCo ED check (ang `flag` ay cross-checked sa `ghz`) at nag-herald ng odd-parity sector (odd na bilang ng 1 sa `ghz`). Ang mga napanatiling `w` bit ay nagbibigay ng Hamming-weight distribution, ng coherence $C$, at ng mga bound sa fidelity $F$ kasama ang $|W_n\\rangle$. Panghuli, ang `exact_reference` ay nagbibigay ng mga ideal na value na hinango sa seksyong Background. (Kung ang mga circuit ay ginawa gamit ang `feedforward=False`, unang ina-apply ng `postselect` ang mga GHZ correction na iniwan para sa postprocessing. Tingnan ang Step 1 sa ibaba.)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Maliit na simulator na halimbawa {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, run the protocol in simulation for $n = 6$ W qubits (12 qubits in total), in two ways:\n"
msgstr "Una, patakbuhin ang protocol sa simulation para sa $n = 6$ na W qubit (12 qubit sa kabuuan), sa dalawang paraan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Expected reference:** the ideal values derived in the Background section, computed by `exact_reference`. `StatevectorSampler` cannot run circuits that contain classical feedforward (`if_test`), so this example also runs the logical (untranspiled) circuits on the noiseless `AerSimulator`. This checks both the circuits and the postprocessing: without noise, every shot should pass the DisCo ED check, and the results should agree with the expected values up to shot noise.\n"
msgstr "**Inaasahang reference:** ang mga ideal na value na hinango sa seksyong Background, na kinukwenta ng `exact_reference`. Hindi kayang patakbuhin ng `StatevectorSampler` ang mga circuit na may classical feedforward (`if_test`), kaya pinapatakbo rin ng halimbawang ito ang mga logical (hindi pa na-transpile) na circuit sa noiseless na `AerSimulator`. Sinusuri nito pareho ang mga circuit at ang postprocessing: kapag walang noise, dapat pumasa ang bawat shot sa DisCo ED check, at dapat tumugma ang mga resulta sa mga inaasahang value hanggang sa shot noise.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Noisy run:** [local testing mode](/guides/local-testing-mode) with `FakeMiami`, a fake Nighthawk backend with the same square lattice as the hardware example. This shows how far a hardware-like result drifts from the expected one, and how much of the gap DisCo ED recovers.\n"
msgstr "**Noisy na run:** [local testing mode](/guides/local-testing-mode) gamit ang `FakeMiami`, isang fake na Nighthawk backend na may parehong square lattice gaya ng hardware na halimbawa. Ipinapakita nito kung gaano kalayo ang resultang parang hardware mula sa inaasahan, at kung gaano karami sa agwat ang naibabalik ng DisCo ED.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Step 1: I-map ang mga classical na input sa isang quantum na problema {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit uses two lines of $n$ qubits: the GHZ line `q_ghz`, which serves as the distributed control, and the W line `q_w`, which ends up in the W state. The circuit has three pieces, one for each stage of the protocol.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang circuit ng dalawang linya ng $n$ qubit: ang GHZ line na `q_ghz`, na nagsisilbing distributed control, at ang W line na `q_w`, na nauuwi sa W state. May tatlong bahagi ang circuit, isa para sa bawat yugto ng protocol.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**1. Prepare the GHZ state.** `prepare_ghz` splits the GHZ line into the staggered patches $[0], [1, 2], [3, 4], \\ldots$ (the last patch also takes the final qubit) and prepares a small GHZ state in each patch. It then fuses neighboring patches. A CNOT copies the parity $Z_aZ_b$ of the two qubits on either side of a boundary onto $b$, the first qubit of the right patch. Qubit $b$ is then measured into `fusion`, reset, and re-entangled with its patch. Finally, the feedforward applies $X$ to every qubit of patch $k$ if the parity of the first $k$ fusion outcomes is odd. The conditions are built with `expr.bit_xor`, so all corrections happen in one round of feedforward.\n"
msgstr "**1. Ihanda ang GHZ state.** Hinahati ng `prepare_ghz` ang GHZ line sa mga staggered na patch na $[0], [1, 2], [3, 4], \\ldots$ (ang huling patch ay kasama rin ang huling qubit) at naghahanda ng maliit na GHZ state sa bawat patch. Pagkatapos ay pinagsasama nito ang magkakatabing patch. Kinokopya ng isang CNOT ang parity na $Z_aZ_b$ ng dalawang qubit sa magkabilang panig ng boundary papunta sa $b$, ang unang qubit ng kanang patch. Ang qubit na $b$ ay sinusukat papunta sa `fusion`, ni-reset, at muling ine-entangle sa patch nito. Panghuli, ina-apply ng feedforward ang $X$ sa bawat qubit ng patch $k$ kung odd ang parity ng unang $k$ na fusion outcome. Ang mga kondisyon ay binuo gamit ang `expr.bit_xor`, kaya lahat ng correction ay nangyayari sa isang round ng feedforward.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every correction is an $X$, and the rest of the circuit only moves it around: the CZ layer turns $X_{g_j}$ into $X_{g_j}Z_{w_j}$, and the GHZ readout carries it onto known bits. So the measurement statistics are the same if, instead of applying the corrections on the device, you apply them to the measured bits afterward (`deferred_corrections` and `postselect` in the Setup cell). This is called tracking the *Pauli frame*. Note that it does not prepare the W state on the device; it only reproduces the outcomes that the device would have measured. `prepare_ghz` therefore applies the corrections in real time by default (`feedforward=True`). Setting `feedforward=False` is a useful diagnostic: it removes the wait for the fusion outcomes to reach the controller and come back, during which the whole GHZ line idles, so comparing the two settings shows how much error that wait adds.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat correction ay isang $X$, at ang natitirang bahagi ng circuit ay gumagalaw lang nito: ginagawa ng CZ layer ang $X_{g_j}$ bilang $X_{g_j}Z_{w_j}$, at dinadala ito ng GHZ readout sa mga kilalang bit. Kaya pareho ang measurement statistics kung, sa halip na i-apply ang mga correction sa device, ia-apply mo ang mga ito sa mga nasukat na bit pagkatapos (`deferred_corrections` at `postselect` sa Setup cell). Tinatawag itong pag-track ng *Pauli frame*. Tandaan na hindi nito inihahanda ang W state sa device; ginagaya lang nito ang mga outcome na masusukat sana ng device. Kaya ina-apply ng `prepare_ghz` ang mga correction nang real time bilang default (`feedforward=True`). Ang pagtatakda ng `feedforward=False` ay isang kapaki-pakinabang na diagnostic: inaalis nito ang paghihintay na makarating ang mga fusion outcome sa controller at bumalik, kung kailan nakatengga ang buong GHZ line, kaya ipinapakita ng paghahambing ng dalawang setting kung gaano karaming error ang idinadagdag ng paghihintay na iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**2. Seed and couple the W qubits.** `couple_w_qubits` rotates every W qubit with $R_Y(\\theta)$, where $\\theta = 2\\arcsin\\sqrt{\\delta/n}$ so that $p = \\delta/n$. It then applies $CZ(g_j, w_j)$ on every rung of the ladder, which is the controlled-$Z^{\\otimes n}$ of the distributed Hadamard test. The circuit applies the rotations after the GHZ preparation, just before the CZ layer. That way, the W qubits wait in $|0\\rangle$, which does not decay, during the slow mid-circuit measurements and feedforward.\n"
msgstr "**2. I-seed at i-couple ang mga W qubit.** Ini-rotate ng `couple_w_qubits` ang bawat W qubit gamit ang $R_Y(\\theta)$, kung saan $\\theta = 2\\arcsin\\sqrt{\\delta/n}$ kaya $p = \\delta/n$. Pagkatapos ay ina-apply nito ang $CZ(g_j, w_j)$ sa bawat rung ng ladder, na siyang controlled-$Z^{\\otimes n}$ ng distributed Hadamard test. Ina-apply ng circuit ang mga rotation pagkatapos ng GHZ preparation, bago lang ang CZ layer. Sa ganoong paraan, naghihintay ang mga W qubit sa $|0\\rangle$, na hindi nagde-decay, habang may mabagal na mid-circuit measurement at feedforward.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**3. Read out the GHZ state with DisCo ED.** `readout_ghz` measures the logical $\\bar X$ of the GHZ state. With `check=None`, every GHZ qubit is measured in the $X$ basis into `ghz`. With `\"explicit\"` or `\"implicit\"`, the GHZ line is split into the pairs $(2k, 2k+1)$, as described in the Background section. The root $r = 2k+1$ is measured into bit $k$ of `ghz`, and the check $c = 2k$ into bit $k$ of `flag`. The only difference between the two checks is the second CNOT.\n"
msgstr "**3. Basahin ang GHZ state gamit ang DisCo ED.** Sinusukat ng `readout_ghz` ang logical na $\\bar X$ ng GHZ state. Kapag `check=None`, bawat GHZ qubit ay sinusukat sa $X$ basis papunta sa `ghz`. Kapag `\"explicit\"` o `\"implicit\"`, hinahati ang GHZ line sa mga pares na $(2k, 2k+1)$, gaya ng inilarawan sa seksyong Background. Ang root na $r = 2k+1$ ay sinusukat papunta sa bit $k$ ng `ghz`, at ang check na $c = 2k$ papunta sa bit $k$ ng `flag`. Ang tanging pagkakaiba ng dalawang check ay ang pangalawang CNOT.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`build_w_state_circuit` puts the three pieces together, then measures the W qubits in the requested basis. The barriers only separate the stages in the circuit drawing.\n"
msgstr "Pinagsasama ng `build_w_state_circuit` ang tatlong bahagi, pagkatapos ay sinusukat ang mga W qubit sa hiniling na basis. Pinaghihiwalay lang ng mga barrier ang mga yugto sa drawing ng circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example builds nine circuits for $n = 6$: three DisCo ED modes, each measured in three bases. The $Z$-basis circuits give the Hamming-weight distribution, and the $X$- and $Y$-basis circuits give the coherence $C$. The cell below draws the implicit-check circuit with $Z$-basis measurements. From left to right, you can see the GHZ preparation, with its two fusion measurements and the feedforward corrections (`if_test` blocks); the rotations and the CZ rungs; and the paired DisCo ED readout. Note that the two-qubit depth of each stage does not depend on $n$.\n"
msgstr "Gumagawa ang halimbawang ito ng siyam na circuit para sa $n = 6$: tatlong DisCo ED mode, bawat isa ay sinusukat sa tatlong basis. Ang mga $Z$-basis na circuit ay nagbibigay ng Hamming-weight distribution, at ang mga $X$- at $Y$-basis na circuit ay nagbibigay ng coherence $C$. Ang cell sa ibaba ay gumuguhit ng implicit-check na circuit na may $Z$-basis na measurement. Mula kaliwa pakanan, makikita ang GHZ preparation, kasama ang dalawang fusion measurement nito at ang mga feedforward correction (mga `if_test` block); ang mga rotation at ang mga CZ rung; at ang pares-paresong DisCo ED readout. Tandaan na hindi nakadepende sa $n$ ang two-qubit depth ng bawat yugto.\n"

