# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Step 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa pagpapatakbo sa quantum hardware {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile the circuits for `FakeMiami`. The snapshot behind this fake backend does not list the `reset` and `if_else` instructions that real Nighthawk processors support, so the code below adds them to its target first. The simulator then models reset as noiseless.\n"
msgstr "I-transpile ang mga circuit para sa `FakeMiami`. Hindi inililista ng snapshot sa likod ng fake backend na ito ang mga instruction na `reset` at `if_else` na sinusuportahan ng mga totoong Nighthawk processor, kaya idinadagdag muna ng code sa ibaba ang mga ito sa target nito. Imomodelo naman ng simulator ang reset bilang noiseless.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The target qubit layout is a ladder: the GHZ line is a path of $n$ connected qubits, and each W qubit is a neighbor of its GHZ partner, joined by a CZ rung. Many ladders fit on the square lattice, and qubit quality varies across the device, so `choose_layout` picks one from the backend's calibration data. It estimates the expected number of errors of a ladder: the CZ errors of the edges it uses, the readout errors of every measurement, and the dephasing of the GHZ line while the fusion qubits are measured. It grows candidate GHZ lines one qubit at a time, keeping the cheapest, then gives each line its best W qubits. The code passes this layout to the transpiler for all nine circuits, so that every mode runs on the same physical qubits and the comparison between modes is fair. No SWAP gates are needed, and the CZ depth is 4 without error detection and 5 with it. The extra layer is the readout CNOT. The second CNOT of the implicit check merges with the first one into a single CZ, so the implicit and explicit circuits have the same CZ count.\n"
msgstr "Ang target na qubit layout ay isang ladder: ang GHZ line ay isang path ng $n$ na konektadong qubit, at ang bawat W qubit ay kapitbahay ng GHZ partner nito, na pinagdugtong ng isang CZ rung. Maraming ladder ang kasya sa square lattice, at nag-iiba ang kalidad ng qubit sa buong device, kaya pumipili ang `choose_layout` ng isa mula sa calibration data ng backend. Tinatantya nito ang inaasahang bilang ng error ng isang ladder: ang mga CZ error ng mga edge na ginagamit, ang mga readout error ng bawat measurement, at ang dephasing ng GHZ line habang sinusukat ang mga fusion qubit. Pinapalaki nito ang mga kandidatong GHZ line nang isang qubit bawat beses, at pinapanatili ang pinakamura, pagkatapos ay binibigyan ang bawat line ng pinakamahusay nitong W qubit. Ipinapasa ng code ang layout na ito sa transpiler para sa lahat ng siyam na circuit, para tumakbo ang bawat mode sa parehong pisikal na qubit at patas ang paghahambing ng mga mode. Walang kailangang SWAP gate, at ang CZ depth ay 4 kapag walang error detection at 5 kapag mayroon. Ang dagdag na layer ay ang readout CNOT. Ang pangalawang CNOT ng implicit check ay nagsasama sa una bilang isang CZ, kaya pareho ang bilang ng CZ ng implicit at explicit na circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Step 3: Patakbuhin gamit ang mga Qiskit primitive {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compute the expected reference with `exact_reference`, then run the circuits with `SamplerV2` in two ways: the logical circuits on a noiseless `AerSimulator`, and the transpiled circuits on `FakeMiami`, with its noise model. Each `(check, basis)` circuit is one PUB. Store the results in a dictionary with the same keys as `circuits`.\n"
msgstr "Kwentahin ang inaasahang reference gamit ang `exact_reference`, pagkatapos ay patakbuhin ang mga circuit gamit ang `SamplerV2` sa dalawang paraan: ang mga logical na circuit sa noiseless na `AerSimulator`, at ang mga na-transpile na circuit sa `FakeMiami`, kasama ang noise model nito. Ang bawat `(check, basis)` na circuit ay isang PUB. I-store ang mga resulta sa isang dictionary na may parehong key gaya ng `circuits`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Step 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang resulta sa nais na classical na format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each mode, the table reports:\n"
msgstr "Para sa bawat mode, iniuulat ng table ang:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "the **acceptance**: the fraction of shots that pass the DisCo ED check\n"
msgstr "ang **acceptance**: ang bahagi ng mga shot na pumasa sa DisCo ED check\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "the **success**: the fraction of accepted shots that herald the odd-parity sector, which should match the projection success rate $r_s$\n"
msgstr "ang **success**: ang bahagi ng mga tinanggap na shot na nag-herald ng odd-parity sector, na dapat tumugma sa projection success rate na $r_s$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**P(w=1)** and **C**, computed from the shots that are both accepted and heralded\n"
msgstr "**P(w=1)** at **C**, na kinukwenta mula sa mga shot na parehong tinanggap at na-herald\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**F**: a lower and an upper bound on the fidelity with $|W_n\\rangle$, computed from the Hamming-weight distribution and $C$ (see `fidelity_bounds`). The paper reports this fidelity, so it is the number to compare with Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr "**F**: isang lower at isang upper bound sa fidelity kasama ang $|W_n\\rangle$, na kinukwenta mula sa Hamming-weight distribution at $C$ (tingnan ang `fidelity_bounds`). Iniuulat ng paper ang fidelity na ito, kaya ito ang numerong ihahambing sa Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The expected value of $C$ is slightly above 1. This is because the small weight-3 component of the approximate W state has $C = 3(n-3)/(n-1) > 1$ (see the comment in `exact_reference`).\n"
msgstr "Ang inaasahang value ng $C$ ay bahagyang higit sa 1. Ito ay dahil ang maliit na weight-3 na component ng approximate na W state ay may $C = 3(n-3)/(n-1) > 1$ (tingnan ang comment sa `exact_reference`).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, the noiseless run. Every shot passes the DisCo ED check (acceptance = 1), and all three modes agree with the expected reference up to shot noise. Only about 900 of the 4,000 shots per circuit are heralded, so $C$ carries a statistical uncertainty of about $\\pm 0.03$, and deviations of a few hundredths are expected. So the error detection never discards a good shot, and the circuits and postprocessing are correct.\n"
msgstr "Una, ang noiseless na run. Pumapasa ang bawat shot sa DisCo ED check (acceptance = 1), at tumutugma ang lahat ng tatlong mode sa inaasahang reference hanggang sa shot noise. Humigit-kumulang 900 lang sa 4,000 shot kada circuit ang na-herald, kaya may statistical uncertainty na humigit-kumulang $\\pm 0.03$ ang $C$, at inaasahan ang mga paglihis na ilang daan-daan. Kaya hindi kailanman itinatapon ng error detection ang magandang shot, at tama ang mga circuit at ang postprocessing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now the noisy run. The plot shows the Hamming-weight distribution of the postselected W state (left), and the two observables $P(w=1)$ and $C$ (right), compared with the expected values (gray).\n"
msgstr "Ngayon, ang noisy na run. Ipinapakita ng plot ang Hamming-weight distribution ng postselected na W state (kaliwa), at ang dalawang observable na $P(w=1)$ at $C$ (kanan), kumpara sa mga inaasahang value (gray).\n"

