# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 1–3: Map, optimize, and submit {#steps-13-map-optimize-and-submit}"
msgstr "Mga Step 1–3: I-map, i-optimize, at i-submit {#steps-13-map-optimize-and-submit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, put these steps together at a larger scale and submit the job to real quantum hardware. Prepare a W state on $n = 10$ qubits, using 20 qubits of `ibm_chicago`, a Nighthawk processor. The functions are the same as in the small-scale example; only $n$, $\\delta$, the backend, and the number of shots change. Because the protocol has constant depth, the transpiled circuits have the same CZ depth as for $n = 6$.\n"
msgstr "Dito, pagsamahin ang mga hakbang na ito sa mas malaking scale at i-submit ang job sa totoong quantum hardware. Maghanda ng W state sa $n = 10$ na qubit, gamit ang 20 qubit ng `ibm_chicago`, isang Nighthawk processor. Pareho ang mga function sa maliit na halimbawa; ang $n$, $\\delta$, ang backend, at ang bilang ng shot lang ang nagbabago. Dahil constant ang depth ng protocol, pareho ang CZ depth ng mga na-transpile na circuit sa $n = 6$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three settings matter on hardware:\n"
msgstr "Tatlong setting ang mahalaga sa hardware:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Layout.** `choose_layout` picks the 20 qubits from the current calibration, and all nine circuits run on them.\n"
msgstr "**Layout.** Pinipili ng `choose_layout` ang 20 qubit mula sa kasalukuyang calibration, at lahat ng siyam na circuit ay tumatakbo sa mga ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Fast readout and dynamical decoupling.** `fast_readout` swaps in the device's faster measure and measure-and-reset instructions, and the GHZ line runs a dynamical decoupling sequence while the fusion qubits are measured.\n"
msgstr "**Mabilis na readout at dynamical decoupling.** Pinapalitan ng `fast_readout` ang measure at measure-and-reset na instruction ng device ng mas mabilis na bersyon, at nagpapatakbo ang GHZ line ng dynamical decoupling sequence habang sinusukat ang mga fusion qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A larger $\\delta$.** On hardware, some even-parity shots pass the herald (see the DisCo ED section). Most of them have weight 0, and their size relative to the weight-1 component scales as $1/\\delta$. A larger $\\delta$ dilutes them, at the cost of more weight-3 contamination (about $\\delta^2/6$). This tutorial uses $\\delta = 0.6$, which gives an ideal fidelity of 0.95 and $r_s \\approx 0.36$.\n"
msgstr "**Mas malaking $\\delta$.** Sa hardware, may ilang even-parity na shot na pumapasa sa herald (tingnan ang seksyong DisCo ED). Karamihan sa mga ito ay may weight 0, at ang laki nila kumpara sa weight-1 na component ay sumusunod sa $1/\\delta$. Pinapalabnaw sila ng mas malaking $\\delta$, kapalit ng mas maraming weight-3 contamination (humigit-kumulang $\\delta^2/6$). Gumagamit ang tutorial na ito ng $\\delta = 0.6$, na nagbibigay ng ideal na fidelity na 0.95 at $r_s \\approx 0.36$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Only a fraction of the shots are kept, so this run uses 20,000 shots per circuit.\n"
msgstr "Isang bahagi lang ng mga shot ang pinapanatili, kaya gumagamit ang run na ito ng 20,000 shot kada circuit.\n"

